module gunbc.plans.p4_home_serving_power_semantics

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import std.types { Duration, NonEmptyStr, Timestamp }
import std.nat { Nat }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetirement, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock, MarkdownListItem, TableBlock, CodeBlock, MarkdownAlignment, AlignNone }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { h2, h3, p, li, ul, ol, cell, row, quote }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

// The carrier for the P4 home-serving watt-semantics decision. DESIGN §1: "A plan's
// authority is its `.dag` carrier; generated plan markdown whose only consumer is
// ProjectDocumentation is not a checkout artifact." So there is deliberately NO
// docs/plans/*.md for this plan — the `PlanIsAuthorityOnly` projection below is what
// says so, and the generated-artifact gate treats a committed projection of it as stale.
//
// Two conventions this carrier holds itself to, because a decision document is where
// they are easiest to violate:
//   * DESIGN §3 — every code reference names the module and symbol, never a file:line.
//     (One citation in an earlier draft drifted out from under its own line number while
//     the document was being written, which is the failure that rule names.)
//   * DESIGN §6 — where a claim rests on a count, the count is named as the command that
//     re-derives it, not transcribed as a number. Transcribed counts rot unreachably;
//     the file-count claims in an earlier draft had already gone stale twice.
fn p4_home_serving_power_semantics_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "Citation witnesses re-read the tree at `git rev-parse origin/main`. P4 separates a catalog power ceiling from an applied run limit before card × power selection. The typed ruling and fleet-observation projections below establish standing; they do not select cards or authorize a watt value. [Original measurements, alternatives and review receipts](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/06d3c1c3149a7420c4a548b9aba9b15c721c635d/dag/gunbc/plans/p4_home_serving_power_semantics.dag) preserves the audit trail."),
    h2(text: "The request and existing selection"),
    p(text: "home_serving_accelerator_field_p4_frontier requires a real fold consuming home_serving_add_in_card_catalog_rows as candidates and home_serving_reference_sxm_catalog_rows only as references; an existence witness cannot close it. gunbc.serving.home_serving_candidate_field.select_home_serving_candidate now consumes both, and the_frontier_is_bound_to_the_fold_that_consumes_it checks the bound reference. The remaining barrier is evidence, not another list. home_serving_cell_identity derives cand_<card>_at_<rung>w from citation anchor and offered rung; do not hand-author parallel card/rung chains. Applied figures enter through home_serving_power_admission_applied on an admitted pair; ceilings through the board’s board_power figure citation and gpu_board_power_ceiling, never positional labels."),
    h2(text: "Two figures and their standing"),
    p(text: "Catalog correction (2026-10-28): GpuDeviceCatalogRow carries no power figure; both candidate and reference rosters are List<GpuBoardAdmission>. `extdeps.gpu.types::GpuBoardCatalogFacts.board_power: GpuBoardPowerSpecification?` carries the board specification; gpu_board_power_ceiling reads its Watt ceiling. `gunbc.spark.serving_performance_subject::ServingAcceleratorRealization.applied_power_limit` is a run-scoped setting: same unit, different subject, related only by home_serving_power_policy. The original audit compared Workstation/Max-Q at 600/300 W and PRO 5000 at 48/72 GiB with 300 W; those are decision-time readings, preserved in the linked capture. gpu_catalog_row_eq keys cited vendor + SKU, not Package×VRAM×TDP. PRO 6000 boards have PcieAddInBoard attachment; SXM reference boards have absent board_power. Keep device and board identities when comparing operating points."),
    p(text: "The original fixture audit found no applied-power reading in fixtures/gpu_bench/pro6000ws_600w_v2/: the JSONL has no power key, auto.log/results have no watt/power/tdp field, and “600” occurs in run labels and timestamp digits. A run name is not a watt. The original NVML module exposed memory, not power; the applied-limit field had no production producer, presence/wire readers and one value comparison. Re-derive those scoped findings from the source/fixture witnesses rather than reusing dated counts as current fact."),
    p(text: "A (catalog-only) restates a ceiling already on the board and cannot express a 600 W card at 400 W. B (applied-only) lacks a reading and would rank an inferred label. C keeps both: a required cited ceiling, plus AppliedLimitUnread or AppliedLimitGrounded { limit: Watt, standing: CitedFigureStanding }; PowerPolicyUnread refuses. No applied watt enters without standing, and applied_limit ≤ tdp_watts is a hard pre-Pareto condition. A future candidate without a ceiling refuses, never silently omits it. The candidate/reference witness checks cited ceilings, absent-ceiling references and catalog population completeness."),
    p(text: "Reuse extdeps.external_authority.CitedFigureStanding: CitedToAuthority, TranscribedUncited with read obligation, ObservedByReceipt. cited_figure_read_obligation supplies the unresolved obligation. Only ObservedReceipt is sealed; ExternalAuthority is open. Thus C makes missing standing unwritable, not a false citation unwritable. Use named standing rows, pin exact authority.uri.locator, and review that the cited document states the figure. P1 review 79389 repaired a product-page citation to the actual Workstation datasheet. Repository measurements use the observed arm, not cheap inline CitedToAuthority. Spark’s 140 W whole-SoC figure belongs to the system, never the nested GPU device."),
    p(text: "Selection consumes std.pareto.SelectionAxis/ParetoEntry and std.decision.RealizationSelectionResult, including SelectedWithin with SelectionReceipt and SelectionNeedsEvidence; no parallel chooser. Exclude hard violations before ranking. C starts AppliedLimitUnread and preserves catalog-only/observed-applied cases without promoting a bet."),
    h2(text: "Warm evidence and construction obligations"),
    p(text: "Bind admitted receipt identity, sole-constructor ServingPerformanceSubject, std.measure.TokensPerSecond (or MilliTokensPerSecond) and GpuBenchWarmStanding in one value. Reuse SubjectBoundCacheFit and ServingPromotionEvidence/ServingPromotionReceipts patterns: callers supply receipts, not the verdict, and binding is checked again at use. A bare Nat is not a rate."),
    p(text: "benchmark_warm_capacity_violation_read_as_engine_performance already requires P4 to fund only WarmValid and excludes proven warm-policy failures through the admitted constructor. The original GpuBenchWarmStanding coproduct and mint functions were unsealed: fold witnesses did not prohibit a hand-constructed WarmValid. Use a sealed RECORD with one admit_callers-gated mint; sealing a coproduct arm is not available. observed_receipt self-admission is a named external-authority change requiring review, not merely a call."),
    p(text: "sole_constructor_construction_diags compares source file paths although its diagnostic says defining module; `v1.compiler.infer::constructor_admission_diags_from_lookup` instead compares caller declaration coordinates. The emitted compiler controls include unauthorized constructor-as-function-value. Exact admitted decl_ref(module_path, decl_name) and the actual call must be pinned: synthetic admit_callers roster tests establish entry shape/admission, not that a real roster entry has a live caller. The final mint home is gunbc.serving.home_serving_candidate_field.select_home_serving_candidate, superseding the provisional accelerator-field mint name."),
    p(text: "The committed warm receipt remains WarmCapacityUnread while extdeps.ninfer.replayed_tokens_total is TranscribedUncited. Ground the counter; do not soften the fold. An observed grounding fold takes no arguments and reads committed in-corpus bytes. If those bytes are transcribed, name that boundary and its dissolution trigger rather than claiming the substrate independently checks it."),
    h2(text: "Outcome: what was decided, by whom, and what is still open"),
    p(text: p4_ruling_sentence()),
    p(text: p4_branch_sentence()),
    p(text: "The recorded differential ran separate scratch mutations through claim_batch --entry dag/test/claim/home_serving_power_policy_witness.dag: inverted comparison, unsealed type/roster removal, uncited ceiling treated as grounded, split applied reading, and conflated two figures. Each reddened a claim; conflation reddened its own claim alone. Both kill-matrix negative arms and the positive control’s unresolvable import also reddened after review 82779. No committed mutation harness exists; reproducing this receipt requires repeating those edits."),
    p(text: p4_fleet_sentence()),
    ul(items: p4_trace_condition_rows()),
    p(text: "The seal wording ledger #14472 records a LATENT fork: claim_batch at 891198514b8 refused two module headers in one file (module index refused) and one module name in two files (module-path collision), with probe shapes asserted. A change relaxing either refusal triggers the issue. Do not silently reword “module” to “file”: settle the intended seal boundary with its own test in the same change. Neither branch authorship nor this plan supplies merge authority."),
  ]
}

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// THE STATUS HALF OF THE DECISION, TYPED (§4c: an event, a status, a count or a dissolution
// condition belongs in a carrier, not in prose). Three paragraphs here used to be narrative, and
// each was a snapshot that went false on its own schedule: the head of a branch under push, the
// merge state of a PR, and whether the operator had answered an ask. DESIGN §6 — "name the
// instrument, never transcribe its output" — is why the PR heads and merge states are NOT
// recorded here at all: they move under every push and every review, and a document that quoted
// `gh pr view` would be false by tomorrow. What IS recorded is what cannot drift silently, either
// because a claim re-reads the tree (the trace conditions, the unresolved module) or because the
// event is fixed in time (who asked, when, what closed it). The sentences the reader sees are
// RENDERED FROM these rows, the idiom `demand_restatement_follow_up` establishes: derived from the
// rows, never authored in the body, so prose and fact cannot diverge while the claim stays green.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

type P4RulingRecord {
  ask_id: String
  asked_at: Timestamp
  // A duration, not a string. The close rule does arithmetic on this value, and "15 minutes"
  // as text could not be compared against anything; std.types.Duration is the named carrier
  // (Int seconds, range min 0) and the words the reader sees are rendered from it below.
  window_seconds: Duration
  decided_by: String
  recorded_by: String
  recorded_at: String
  standing_words: String
  license: String
  overturn: String
}

data p4_ruling_record: P4RulingRecord = P4RulingRecord {
  ask_id: "msg_2b573b87",
  asked_at: "2026-10-19T11:46:45Z" as Timestamp,
  window_seconds: 900,
  decided_by: "the close rule, not the operator",
  recorded_by: "manager stern-bat-401",
  recorded_at: "2026-10-19T12:01:35Z" as Timestamp,
  standing_words: "by default, not by endorsement",
  license: "the shape, not a number",
  overturn: "an operator answer naming A or B reopens it",
}

// Rendered FROM the Duration; the unit lives in the type, not in a stored string.
fn p4_window_words() -> String {
  join([to_string(p4_ruling_record.window_seconds / 60), " minutes"], "")
}

fn p4_ruling_sentence() -> String {
  join([
    "**The ruling was C, and it stands ", p4_ruling_record.standing_words, "** — decided by ",
    p4_ruling_record.decided_by, ". The escalation (ask `", p4_ruling_record.ask_id, "`, filed ",
    p4_ruling_record.asked_at, ", recommendation C) drew no operator answer within the ",
    p4_window_words(), ", so it closed with the recommendation approved; ",
    p4_ruling_record.recorded_by, " recorded it at ", p4_ruling_record.recorded_at, ". Read that as a default: it licenses ",
    p4_ruling_record.license, ", and ", p4_ruling_record.overturn, ". Nothing in the shipped model reads an operator ",
    "preference as a fact, and no mint, fold or witness branches on who decided this.",
  ], "")
}

type P4BranchRecord {
  // A PR number is a number, and this is the ONE place it lives: the instrument string is
  // derived from it (p4_pr_state_instrument), so the number can no longer disagree with itself.
  pr: Nat
  branch: NonEmptyStr
  model_files: String
  tree_invariant: String
  heal_artifact: String
}

data p4_branch_record: P4BranchRecord = P4BranchRecord {
  pr: 14463,
  branch: "p4-home-serving-power-policy" as NonEmptyStr,
  model_files: "`dag/gunbc/serving/home_serving_power_policy.dag` and its claim witness",
  tree_invariant: "the_citations_in_the_plan_resolve_against_the_declaration_census",
  heal_artifact: "`src/v1/stage0/src/std_decimal.rs`, auto-committed by the CI heal job as a re-emit of `fixed_point_trimmed_wire` — a generated function from `std.decimal` that this module never touches, after that artifact drifted on main independently of the branch",
}

// Derived from the typed PR number, so the number cannot appear twice and disagree with itself.
fn p4_pr_state_instrument() -> String {
  join(["gh pr view ", to_string(p4_branch_record.pr), " --json state,headRefOid"], "")
}

fn p4_branch_sentence() -> String {
  join([
    "**The C model was authored on a branch** (PR #"
    + to_string(p4_branch_record.pr) + ") on `", p4_branch_record.branch as String, "` as ",
    p4_branch_record.model_files,
    ". Its merge state and head are deliberately ",
    "not transcribed — both move under every push, and a pushed branch is not a merged change; `",
    p4_pr_state_instrument(), "` answers that, today. Whether the model is on *this* tree is likewise ",
    "not asserted by this sentence: it is enforced by execution. `", p4_branch_record.tree_invariant,
    "` resolves `gunbc.serving.home_serving_power_policy` against the census on the head the claim runs ",
    "against, and pairs it with a same-module declaration that exists nowhere, so the check can answer no; ",
    "if this paragraph ever goes stale the claim goes red instead of the sentence rotting quietly. The mint, ",
    "the roster and the refusal described below are the merged module's own behaviour. ",
    "One file GitHub listed on that branch was not authored work: ", p4_branch_record.heal_artifact, ".",
  ], "")
}

// THE FLEET OBSERVATION. The operator answered the ask on 2026-10-20: no host carries a GPU yet, so
// cards and slots are empty as FACT, and P4 must refuse typed rather than select until a GPU-presence
// observation exists; software traces are the PREFERRED presence evidence, but RELIABILITY-CONDITIONAL,
// with three named conditions and an explicit instruction to model it as an observation, not a constant.
// So this row is an observation with a STANDING, and the standing is derived: `p4_trace_is_reliable`
// reads the fixture bytes on every run and only all-true conditions make it reliable. Today two are
// false, which is why presence is refused and nothing downstream may select a card.
type P4TraceCondition {
  name: String
  met: Bool
  what_it_would_show: String
  instrument: String
}

type P4FleetObservation {
  answered_at: Timestamp
  answered_via: String
  gpu_hosts: String
  cards: String
  slots: String
  preferred_evidence: String
  consequence: String
}

// FRESHNESS: a dated row is one that opens yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss. Measured over the committed bytes by
// the claim, never quoted here.
data p4_trace_freshness: P4TraceCondition = P4TraceCondition {
  name: "freshness",
  met: true,
  what_it_would_show: "the trace was produced at a stated time rather than written down from memory, so it can be set against a run window",
  instrument: "filesystem_read(path: \"fixtures/gpu_bench/pro6000ws_600w_v2/auto.log\") — the claim counts rows opening with a date itself",
}

// PROVENANCE: unmet, and the reason is stated as a search the claim performs. No line in any gpu-bench
// fixture names the tool that wrote it; the tool is INFERRED from the column layout. An inference drawn
// from a header is not provenance, so this condition fails rather than being waived.
data p4_trace_provenance: P4TraceCondition = P4TraceCondition {
  name: "provenance",
  met: false,
  what_it_would_show: "a line that states which tool wrote the file. Today none does, in any of the three fixtures — the tool is inferred from the column layout, and an inference from a header is not provenance",
  instrument: "filesystem_read over all three fixtures/gpu_bench/pro6000ws_600w_v2 files — the claim searches every line for a tool naming itself",
}

// NEGATIVE CONTROL: unmet, and this is the condition the operator named specifically. Every committed
// fixture is a POSITIVE — each one names a device — so none of them can show that a host WITHOUT the
// card produces no trace. Without that half, a trace cannot distinguish "the GPU was there" from
// "someone wrote this file", which is exactly the reliability the operator asked me to show.
data p4_trace_negative_control: P4TraceCondition = P4TraceCondition {
  name: "negative control",
  met: false,
  what_it_would_show: "a committed fixture from a host with no GPU, showing that absence produces no trace. What the tree holds is the other half only: the two table traces print the device-name row and the receipt stream carries the run label on every line, and no fixture anywhere reports an absent device. So nothing in the corpus can distinguish a card that was present from a file that was written",
  instrument: "filesystem_read over all three fixtures/gpu_bench/pro6000ws_600w_v2 files — the claim asserts the device-name row is present in the two table traces (the positive floor, which is what makes the read non-vacuous) and that NO fixture carries an absent-device marker",
}

data p4_fleet_observation: P4FleetObservation = P4FleetObservation {
  answered_at: "2026-10-20" as Timestamp,
  answered_via: "the operator, relayed by manager stern-bat-401",
  gpu_hosts: "none — no host carries a GPU yet",
  cards: "empty as fact, not as a choice",
  slots: "empty as fact, not as a choice",
  preferred_evidence: "a software trace, once shown reliable",
  consequence: "card and power-limit selection stays a typed refusal; the candidate list stays empty",
}

fn p4_trace_conditions() -> List<P4TraceCondition> {
  [p4_trace_freshness, p4_trace_provenance, p4_trace_negative_control]
}

fn p4_trace_is_reliable() -> Bool {
  all(p4_trace_conditions(), c => c.met)
}

fn p4_presence_standing() -> String {
  if p4_trace_is_reliable() {
    "PRESENCE ESTABLISHED — a trace-backed observation may now feed selection"
  } else {
    "REFUSED — presence is not established, so no card and no limit may be selected"
  }
}

fn p4_unmet_condition_names() -> String {
  join(map(filter(p4_trace_conditions(), c => !c.met), c => c.name), ", ")
}

fn p4_fleet_sentence() -> String {
  join([
    "**Fleet facts, from ", p4_fleet_observation.answered_via, " on ", p4_fleet_observation.answered_at, ".** ",
    p4_fleet_observation.gpu_hosts, ": cards are ", p4_fleet_observation.cards, " and slots are ",
    p4_fleet_observation.slots, ", so the instruction is that P4 **refuses typed and never selects** until a ",
    "GPU-presence observation exists — no fleet is fabricated to make the question answerable. The preferred ",
    "presence evidence is ", p4_fleet_observation.preferred_evidence, ", and **the trace this repo holds does not yet ",
    "meet that bar**: the standing that follows is **", p4_presence_standing()
    + "**, and therefore ", p4_fleet_observation.consequence,
    ". Each condition below names the instrument that re-derives it and is re-read on every run by ",
    "`the_gpu_bench_trace_still_falls_short_of_reliable_presence_evidence`; unmet today: ",
    p4_unmet_condition_names(), ". The candidate ceilings themselves are re-derived, not quoted here: the witness ",
    "reads `gunbc.serving.home_serving_accelerator_field::home_serving_add_in_card_catalog_rows` and looks each row up ",
    "in `extdeps.gpu.nvidia`, so their identity comes from the tree on every run. Their STANDING is the finding that ",
    "made C the right call: every one of them is a `CitedToAuthority` figure about a product line, none is a reading of ",
    "a card in a chassis, and **a run's name is not a watt** — `600w` in a run name has no backing reading on either ",
    "carrier, and nothing here admits it.",
  ], "")
}

fn p4_met_word(c: P4TraceCondition) -> String {
  if c.met {
    "MET"
  } else {
    "NOT MET"
  }
}

fn p4_trace_condition_rows() -> List<MarkdownListItem> {
  map(p4_trace_conditions(), c => li(text: join([
    "**", c.name, "** — ", p4_met_word(c), ". It would show ",
    c.what_it_would_show, ". Instrument: ", c.instrument, ".",
  ], "")))
}

data p4_home_serving_power_semantics_plan: Plan = Plan {
  slug: "p4-home-serving-power-semantics",
  title: "P4 home-serving selection: what the watt figure means",
  body: p4_home_serving_power_semantics_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen {
    condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Dissolves when the home-serving card selection fold exists and consumes a `HomeServingPowerAdmission` — the catalog TDP and the applied limit carried as two distinct figures, with an applied limit above the rated power refused — so that the question this document settles (which of the two figures a recorded watt names) has a consumer in the tree rather than only an argument. TWO FACTS, MEASURED, AND NOT CONFLATED. THE MODEL HAS LANDED: `gunbc.serving.home_serving_power_policy` is present on this head and on `origin/main` (re-derive with `git cat-file -e origin/main:dag/gunbc/serving/home_serving_power_policy.dag || echo absent`), and `the_citations_in_the_plan_resolve_against_the_declaration_census` enforces exactly that on the head it runs against — it resolves `gunbc.serving.home_serving_power_policy::HomeServingPowerAdmission` and holds a same-module declaration unresolved, so it answers in both directions and would go red if the module or the lookup rots. THE CONSUMER HAS SINCE LANDED, AND THIS PARAGRAPH IS CORRECTED RATHER THAN QUIETLY REWRITTEN: it used to read \"THE CONSUMER HAS NOT: the selection fold does not exist, as a module or otherwise\", which was true when written and is false now. `gunbc.serving.home_serving_candidate_field::select_home_serving_candidate` exists, imports both roster lists, and READS A VALUE OF THE ADMITS TYPE — it matches `PowerPolicyAdmitted { admission: admitted }` and takes the applied figure through `home_serving_power_admission_applied`, so the two figures are carried distinctly in its types and an applied limit above the card's rated power yields no candidate. Re-derive with `git grep -ln 'gunbc.serving.home_serving_power_policy' -- dag src`, which now lists this document, the policy module, that module's own claim witness, this document's witness, AND `dag/gunbc/serving/home_serving_candidate_field.dag`. ONE HONEST LIMIT ON WHAT THAT PROVES: on today's live path no pair reaches the Admitted arm at all, because the applied rung is a planned sweep value with no power-limit receipt, so all sixteen cells come back as declared gaps. The consumer exists and is wired to carry an admitted pair; the evidence that would let it carry one does not exist yet. Pinned, not narrated, by `test.claim.home_serving_candidate_field_witness` (sixteen cells offered, each with exactly one gap, and no arm of the selection ever a pick). So the dissolution trigger is NOT the merge request #14463 already settled: that trigger fired, and continuing to key on it would be a stall this document does not track. What it waits on is the fold's design — mint name, roster entry, witness — which the open-items list above already carries as undesigned rather than as scheduled. THE FIRED HALF AND THE UNFIRED HALF, STAPLED APART. The consumer half of this trigger HAS fired: the fold exists and consumes an admitted pair as described above, so the sentence that used to close this carrier — \"when the fold exists and carries both figures with that refusal, the reading lives in its types and this document is deleted\" — describes a state the tree now partly reaches, and the deletion is therefore NOT taken on this change: the fold's types carry the reading, but nothing in the tree has yet exercised it, because no power-limit receipt exists for any of these cards and the Admitted arm is unreachable on the live path. So what remains unfired, and what this carrier now waits on, is one artifact and one capability: an operator-applied power-limit RECEIPT for a specific card, cited under an ExternalAuthority, which would let a pair reach `PowerPolicyAdmitted` and be witnessed there rather than only wired. When a claim exists that exercises an admitted pair on a cited receipt, the reading lives in the fold's types and is SEEN there, and this document is deleted; deleting it before then would remove the only place the rejected alternatives (A: read the catalog TDP as the applied limit; B: keep one field and re-document it; D: refuse the question) and their evidence are recorded. Re-derive the unfired half with: `git grep -n 'PowerPolicyAdmitted' -- dag/test/claim`, whose only hits are the policy module's own witness building its own readings, and no claim over a cited receipt."),
  },
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
}
